{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,18]],"date-time":"2026-09-18T07:09:45Z","timestamp":1789715385137,"version":"4.0.1"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Victoria University of Wellington Library","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["AJL"],"abstract":"<jats:p>In this paper we present a Gentzen system for reasoning with contrary-to-duty obligations. The intuition behind the system is that a contrary-to-duty is a special kind of normative exception. The logical machinery to formalise this idea is taken from substructural logics and it is based on the definition of a new non-classical connective capturing the notion of reparational obligation. Then the system is tested against well-known contrary-to-duty paradoxes.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.26686\/ajl.v4i0.1780","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2018,4,15]],"date-time":"2018-04-15T23:26:57Z","timestamp":1523834817000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":57,"title":["Logic of Violations: A Gentzen System for Reasoning with Contrary-To-Duty Obligations"],"prefix":"10.26686","volume":"4","author":[{"given":"Guido","family":"Governatori","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Antonino","family":"Rotolo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"11224","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2022,3,10]]},"container-title":["The Australasian Journal of Logic"],"original-title":[],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/ojs.victoria.ac.nz\/ajl\/article\/download\/1780\/6684","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/ojs.victoria.ac.nz\/ajl\/article\/download\/1780\/6684","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,4,12]],"date-t